A "for" loop is used when you know how many times you want to repeat the loop.  Here’s an example:

for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    printf("Hello, world!\n");
}

This loop will print "Hello, world!" 5 times.

A "while" loop is used when you don’t know how many times you want to repeat the loop, but you know how many conditions you’ll test until they are false.  Here’s an example:

int i = 0;
while (i < 5) {
    printf("Hello, world!\n");
    i++;
}

